---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BurnRateLab from "../../components/BurnRateLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Retirement Burn-Rate Calculator"
  description="Estimate your monthly costs in retirement and see the nest egg you'd need — the flip side of the 4% rule — and whether a portfolio can sustain it."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>What will retirement cost?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The 4% rule works both ways. Instead of asking what a portfolio can pay
      out, start from the other end: estimate what you'll actually spend each
      month, and see how big a nest egg that spending implies — and whether a
      given portfolio can keep up.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <BurnRateLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The 25× shortcut</h2>
      <p>
        Flip the 4% rule around and it becomes a rule of thumb for how much you
        need: divide your annual spending by your withdrawal rate. At 4% that's
        the same as multiplying annual spending by <strong>25</strong> — so
        $50,000 a year implies a $1.25M nest egg. Choose a more cautious 3% and
        it jumps to 33×; a bolder 5% drops it to 20×.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Spending drives everything.</strong> Because of the multiplier,
          trimming $500/month of costs cuts the nest egg you need by roughly
          $150,000 (at 4%). Lowering the number you need can be far easier than
          growing the pile.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>It's a sketch, not a plan.</strong> Real retirements have lumpy,
          rising costs — healthcare especially — and markets don't deliver steady
          returns. Treat the figure as a target to aim at, not a promise.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Educational only, not financial advice.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="burn-rate" />

  <NextTool current="/tools/burn-rate" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .br-group {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin: var(--space-xs) 0 0;
  }
  .br-group:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .br-dot {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .br-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .br-stats > div {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .br-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .br-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .br-breakdown {
    display: flex;
    height: 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  .br-seg {
    height: 100%;
  }
  .br-hero {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .br-hero-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .br-hero-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .br-hero-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .br-verdict h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .br-verdict-line {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .br-verdict-line strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .br-verdict-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
  }
  .br-ok .br-verdict-tag {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .br-short .br-verdict-tag {
    color: var(--color-error);
  }
  .br-verdict {
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .br-ok {
    border-left-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .br-short {
    border-left-color: var(--color-error);
  }
</style>
